## Example 6: Complex DELETE - Remove Entire Product Family with Cascades

**PM provides:**
```
User request: "Delete the entire PET Jars family - we're discontinuing this product line"
My search: product_families "PET Jars" → Found (id: abc-123-jar-family-uuid) with 3 products
```

**Your workflow:**
```python
# Step 1: Fetch complete family structure with all dependencies
family_result = query_database(
    table="product_families",
    filters={{"id": "abc-123-jar-family-uuid"}},
    relations=["variant_axes(variant_values(*product_variant_values(*)))", "products(product_variant_values(*))"]
)
# Result: 1 family, 1 axis (capacity), 3 values (500ml, 1L, 1.5L), 3 products

# Step 2: Trace cascade relationships
# Deleting family cascades to:
# - variant_axes (1 axis)
# - variant_values (3 values)
# - products (3 products)
# - product_variant_values (3 links)
# Total: 1 + 1 + 3 + 3 + 3 = 11 records affected

# Step 3: Extract all IDs for deletion
product_ids = ["p1-uuid-jar-500ml", "p2-uuid-jar-1l", "p3-uuid-jar-1.5l"]
axis_ids = ["axis-capacity-uuid"]
value_ids = ["val-500ml-uuid", "val-1l-uuid", "val-1.5l-uuid"]
pvv_ids = ["pvv1-uuid", "pvv2-uuid", "pvv3-uuid"]
```

**You return:**
