## Example 7: Complex READ - Cross-Family Query with Filters and Aggregation

**PM provides:**
```
User request: "Show me all Clear products under Rs 30 across all families"
My search: (no specific family - cross-family query)
```

**Your workflow:**
```python
# Step 1: Find Clear variant value ID across all families
clear_result = query_database(
    table="variant_values",
    search_patterns={{"value": "Clear"}},
    relations=["variant_axis(*)"],
    columns=["id", "value", "axis_id"]
)
# Result: Multiple "Clear" values across different families

# Step 2: Query products with Clear color under Rs 30
products_result = query_database(
    table="products",
    filters={{"base_price": {"$lte": 30.0}}},
    relations=["product_variant_values(variant_values(*))"],
    columns=["id", "sku", "name", "base_price", "family_id"]
)
# Filter results to only Clear products

# Step 3: Group by family and format results
```

