## Example 10: Bulk DELETE with Multiple Family IDs

**PM provides:**
```
User request: "Delete PET Bottles, PET Jars, and HDPE Containers families"
My search: product_families "PET Bottles" -> 1 match (id: family-uuid-1)
My search: product_families "PET Jars" -> 1 match (id: family-uuid-2)
My search: product_families "HDPE Containers" -> 1 match (id: family-uuid-3)
```

**Your workflow:**
```python
# Step 1: EFFICIENT bulk count query for all 3 families at once
count_result = query_database(
    table="products",
    filters={{
        "family_id": ["family-uuid-1", "family-uuid-2", "family-uuid-3"]  # List = IN operator
    }},
    count_only=True
)
# Returns total products across all 3 families in SINGLE query

# ❌ WRONG: Counting one family at a time
# count1 = query_database(table="products", filters={{"family_id": "family-uuid-1"}}, count_only=True)
# count2 = query_database(table="products", filters={{"family_id": "family-uuid-2"}}, count_only=True)
# count3 = query_database(table="products", filters={{"family_id": "family-uuid-3"}}, count_only=True)
# This makes 3 queries when 1 bulk query would work!

# Step 2: Cascade deletion plan for all 3 families
```

**You return:**
```json
